# Tales (Living Server 1.2, the owner's idea, 2026-11-10): now and then a bot in /faction asks the realm's storyteller for
# a story about a dragon or a boss. A couple of others hush the channel and beg, the teller tells it in a dozen lines with
# a question or two that lead it along, and it ends in a quiet moment. What follows (a related rumour, sometimes a raid
# that really forms) is the engine's, not the scene's (AutonomousTales).
#
# Roles: A asks, B is the TELLER (the engine casts the realm's storyteller there and fills {name_b} with its name),
# C hushes the channel, D begs and asks the questions, E is the one who has heard it too often, F is the newcomer.
# A scene is one telling; each realm tells its own bosses, and Legion and Govannon the way that realm tells them.
# Every tale keeps to the lore files (data/lore/bosses/*.json: the "story" of each). New writing, in chat voice: a teller
# types, it does not recite. Topic "tale_<lore id>"; these scenes never play as ordinary debates.

@kind debate
@realm alb

@topic tale_golestandt
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_golestandt
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} you on? tell the stone dragon one again | hey {name_b}, do the golestandt story, half the realm never heard it
C: oh yes. everyone hush, {name_b} is telling the dartmoor one | shh all, golestandt story incoming
?E: we have heard the dartmoor one a hundred times lol | here we go, the bed of granite again
D: go on {name_b}, please | pleeease {name_b}, the new ppl need to hear about gole
B: fine, fine. sit down then | ok ok. once, and no talking over me
B: south end of dartmoor theres a warm hollow in the granite. the cornish drovers call it the Bed
B: she sleeps in it. and she and the Bed are one stone. hit her anywhere else and the granite takes the blow for her
?F: so thats why nothing hurts her outside the lair? | wait, is that why we only fight her in the hollow
B: thats why. and the giants in the heather are her children. shards of the Bed that got up and walked off
B: back in uther's day a roman lord named articus died out there with his whole house
B: the duke of cornwall's son came home from it alone, burnt, and never once said what he saw
~ 8
D: so how did we even learn her name? | then who named her, if nobody came back?
B: sir arward rode south with thirty, the year the dragons woke. none of them came home
B: but their scribe's journal fell out of a clear sky at prydwen keep. scorched. one word branded on the last page
C: golestandt.
B: an old roman armourer forged heat wards against her. held once. failed the second time
B: camelot's armourers still sell those wards. only in pairs. one for her and one for you
?E: ok that part still gets me | fine, the pairs bit is good, i admit it
~ 25
F: ...i am never going near dartmoor again | i walk past that hollow every day. not anymore
A: thanks {name_b}. gets me every time | told it better than last time, {name_b}

@topic tale_apocalypse
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_apocalypse
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
