A: {name_b}, whats actually at the top of caer sidi? you know the story right | {name_b} tell them about the four riders of caer sidi
C: quiet in faction for a minute, this one is worth it | hush everyone, caer sidi story
D: yes please, i only know there are four horsemen up there | do tell {name_b}, i never got the riders explained
B: alright. top cell of caer sidi. the first one arawn ever built
B: the inconnu say whats in it is the end of the world. arawn couldnt destroy it. you cant end an ending, only keep it
B: so he built the whole turning gaol under that one door to keep it
?F: and the four riders are the guards? | so the horsemen are its jailers
B: not jailers. heralds. fames, bellum, morbus, funus. the four roads to the dead, in the roman tongue
B: and arawn's law binds them. they have to ASK you first. do you challenge fate
B: arthur climbed to them once. he said no. came home with six men. thats the seven the bards sing about
~ 8
D: did anyone ever say yes? | ok so who was the first to answer yes?
B: a company of the dead, when morgana's theft set the prisoners rising. they climbed and said yes
B: he ended every one of them and shut his door again. from the inside
B: the strongest he kept. his harbingers. remade from whoever falls in front of him
?E: cheerful as always {name_b} | and people wonder why i skip caer sidi raids
B: dame ysolde of caer gothwaite took eighty up there. seventy one came home. first time anyone brought him down
B: they say the whole fortress stopped turning for one breath
~ 25
F: stopped turning. wow | and we just... go up there for loot
C: he asks everyone why they came early, they say. i would have no answer

@topic tale_xanxicar
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_xanxicar
@role A type=*
