A: {name_b} whats the thing at the bottom of trollheim? the valkyn wont talk about it | {name_b}, tell the nosdoden one
C: quiet a moment, trollheim story | everyone hush, this one is grim
D: please do, i got lost down there once and heard things | tell it {name_b}, i want to know what i ran from
B: alright. under the deepest holy hall of trollheim the troll fathers raised a mound
B: thats where their dead were given back to the land. and the vaettir, the land spirits, gathered on it
B: the fathers were famous for wisdom. this is where it came from. they asked the dead
?F: and something ate the dead? i see where this goes | let me guess, it didnt stay guarded
B: when the morvalt broke the city the keepers fled. all but one, grimsa. the mound lay open
B: something came to it. jordheim says a dragon. the dwarves say it came UP from below, not down
B: it lay on the mound and fed on the spirits. and the feeding turned its scales to slime and its jaws to tentacles
B: the valkyn named it. nosdoden. death's muzzle
~ 8
D: has anyone fought it and lived? | so what happens if you cut it?
B: ketil grimsson's war band found out. every deep cut let out a host of the dead it had swallowed
B: and every one of ketil's men who died near it stood up again. own face, own craft. fighting for the worm
?E: worst wipe of my life was to my own healer down there | i have been killed by my own guildmate's ghost. true story
B: but a woman named sigrid, tending the wounded, found the one mercy in that place
B: call a fallen man back before the worm is done with him, and he keeps his own spirit. it only takes what is left lying
~ 25
F: so never leave anyone on the floor. got it | rez fast. noted. forever
C: the worm takes only what is left lying. i hate that line

