A: {name_b} what is actually at the bottom of galladoria? the sylvan go quiet when i ask | {name_b}, tell us of the root
C: hush, everyone, {name_b} has the galladoria tale | quiet now, this is the old one. older than us
D: yes, tell it. i have only seen the first rooms | please {name_b}, the whole of it
B: his name is olcasgean. the Root. he was old and angry before the first forest of hy brasil woke
B: the sylvan will not call him a god. the scholars of tir na nog say titan
B: in the Long Pushing the forest grew against him for an age and drove him back to world's end
?F: the forest fought him? the trees themselves? | a forest can push?
B: it set keeper trees to watch him. elro at the edge, who held. and aroon in the hollow below, who rotted
B: but roots do not go away. they go down
B: where his roots ended they made galladoria. a hollow like a mouth, bending the isle's rivers toward it
~ 8
D: and the things living in there now? | so what happened to everything inside?
B: everything that drank that water changed. the broodmother. the conservator. aroon. all of it his now
B: last he took the isle's four elements, wind, water, fire and stone, and set them at the waterfall bridge to guard his sleep
B: hibernia's first three hundred and forty broke on his first law. no one near him who does not stand where he allows
?E: we broke on it too, last month | two spots. he allows two spots. ask our guild
B: orlaith of tir na nog brought a hundred and forty, stood where he allowed, and found he rises as two trunks. each with a full life
B: they cut both
~ 25
F: they go down. i keep hearing that part | two trunks. of course there are two
C: well told {name_b}. the wardens say he has grown hungrier since

@topic tale_black-lady
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_black_lady
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b}, who was the black lady before marfach? someone said she was a singer | {name_b} tell the keener's tale, the sad one
C: quiet a while, friends. the marfach story | hush, this one deserves the silence
D: i would like to hear it {name_b} | tell it, i have only fought her, never understood her
B: she was the eldest of three keeners. hired to sing the chieftain caimheul on, in the hills of breifine
B: a keener sings facing the road. she never looks back at the grave. the eldest had kept that rule forty years
B: but she had raised caimheul in her own house by the lake. his foster mother. and they asked her to keen him anyway
?F: oh no | they asked his own mother to sing him gone
B: she planted an acorn in the floor of his grave. and it sprouted in the dark
B: on the fourth night a kind voice answered her from below. why should you ever stop?
B: and she looked back over her shoulder. and her two sisters looked where she looked
~ 8
D: whose voice was it? | and what answered her?
B: the druids of tir na nog believe it was the calling of the summoners
B: it gave the whole household the grave peace. on the ground where they were laid they can be wounded. beyond it, nothing touches them
B: and when the household came back to the grave, the chieftain was standing
B: the oak went black as bog oak. she gave it her breath. it stands while she returns, and stops when she falls
?E: and her mourners go straight for the healers. every time | they hate menders. anyone who will not let the dead go
~ 25
F: she just could not stop singing | i will think of this next time we are in marfach
A: thank you {name_b} | i always go quiet after that one

# Legion and Govannon, as each realm tells them.

@realm alb

@topic tale_legion
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_legion_alb
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} tell them why its called legion. the df one | {name_b}, the legion story, before the next raid goes down
C: everyone shut up a second, this is the darkness falls one | hush. {name_b} tells legion properly
D: go on {name_b}, i only know it eats bubbles | please, i have always wanted the real story of that thing
B: right. the imps down there will talk for a candle end. this is what they say
B: in the beginning two princes stood equal at the top of the demon court
B: one killed the other. and ate him. and kept his voice
?F: kept his voice?? | it talks with the dead one's voice?
B: and he ate every demon who challenged him after. until he spoke with a hundred voices. so the court named him legion
B: camelot's priests say he is the thing in the gospel that named itself for its number
B: his kingdom has three doors. ours is in camelot hills. they open only for the realm holding the most keeps
~ 8
D: and he really heals when we die? | is it true every death feeds it?
B: every one of us who dies in that room mends him. thats not a saying. thats how he eats
B: he swallows the wards our priests wrap round the fighters too. a friar named ansel had his prayer eaten
B: ansel never prayed a ward again
?E: i watched a raid feed it back to full once. forty deaths | so stop dying in there. simple
B: the roll in camelot names sir aldous fenn as the first of ours to break him
~ 25
F: never prayed again. that one stays with you | i need a minute after that
C: pray for the souls inside it, the priests say. pray later, i say

