A: {name_b} who IS govannon anyway. the summoners hall boss | {name_b}, tell the one about the summoner and his debts
C: shh, summoner's hall story, pay attention | quiet all. {name_b} knows this one from the camelot scholars
D: go on {name_b}, i only know to kill the sacrifice first | tell it, i want to know why there is a sacrifice at all
B: his name is a smith's name, from the old tales of the west. but what he makes is bargains
B: camelot's scholars say he was a mage of the old britons who took that name for himself
B: he came to an empty hall under all three frontiers and filled it with summoners. cunovinda was his first student
?F: under all three? the same hall for every realm? | so the other realms fight him too
B: the same hall. and from it they call the dead of all three realms down through the floors of the frontier dungeons
B: every calling has a price. and govannon pays his debts. thats the part to remember
~ 8
D: so thats what the sacrifice is? | the sacrifice and the demon walking in, is that a payment?
B: its a bargain being struck. a sacrifice and a demon walk to meet at his feet. if both arrive, the price is paid
B: and his old creditor rises out of the floor to collect. the shade of aelfgar. with the war cry that killed him
B: the priests in camelot say aelfgar was one of ours once. a knight
?E: so we are killing a knight's ghost down there. lovely | explains the stun. he was a fighter
B: and hurt govannon badly enough and he sheds the shape he was paid in. the demon steps out whole
B: as if every wound before had been given to someone else
~ 25
F: given to someone else. so who took them | he pays his debts with other people. got it
A: thanks {name_b}. i will never look at the sacrifice the same way

