D: aye tell it. my uncle mined there | go on, i never knew the mine and the hall were one story
B: there is a hall under all three frontiers. an empty sidhe hall, once. a summoner named govannon filled it
B: jordheim's skalds say there is no one under his shape at all. just the shape
B: he and his students call the dead. ours too. down through the floors of the frontier dungeons
?F: he was pulling our dead out of the ground? | our dead answered him?
B: the miners in dodens gruva heard the calling first. their dead began to walk. downward
B: spiritmaster aros bound them where they stood rather than let them go to him
~ 8
D: so aros is not the villain there? | wait. aros was holding them back?
B: he held them back. thats why the mine is full of bound dead. better bound than his
B: govannon pays for every calling. a sacrifice and a demon walk to his feet. if both arrive, his creditor comes to collect
B: and when he is hurt enough the shape comes off. the demon steps out whole
?E: at half. heals to full. i have the scars | the half way trick. every single time
B: like every blow we ever landed went to somebody else
~ 25
F: poor aros | i will look at dodens gruva differently now
A: thats for ormarr's miners. well told {name_b}

@realm hib

@topic tale_grand-summoner-govannon
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_govannon_hib
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b}, why do the druids spit when they say govannon | {name_b} tell of the false sidhe under the frontier
C: quiet now, friends. the summoner's tale | hush. {name_b} tells the one that shames us
D: please. i have seen his face and it troubled me | tell it {name_b}, why does he look like one of the good folk
B: because the face is stolen. the druids of tir na nog say he wears the shape of one of the sidhe
B: the hall he sits in was a sidhe hall. the realms' old meeting place, under all three borders. it stood empty
B: he filled it with summoners. cunovinda, lossren the gatherer, roesia the keeper of pain
?F: and they call the dead from there? | what do they summon
B: the dead of every realm. ours as well. through the floors of the frontier dungeons, down to him
B: the druids believe it was their calling that answered the black lady in marfach
~ 8
D: and the shape? does it ever come off? | what is under the stolen face?
B: he was paid in that shape long ago. hurt him enough and he sheds it. and the demon steps out whole
B: as though every wound before was given to another
B: each calling costs him. a sacrifice and a demon walk to his feet, and if both arrive, something comes to collect
?E: kill the sacrifice first. i say it every raid | dont be fooled by the face. sacrifice dies first
~ 25
F: one of the good folk, worn like a coat | an insult to wear that face
C: the false sidhe. tir na nog will sing when he falls

# Campfire tales (the same stories, short): told in /group by a groupmate while the party rests in or near the place, to the
# player in the group. Two roles: A tells, B listens. Topic "fireside_<lore id>"; played by AutonomousTales, never in /faction.

@realm alb

@topic fireside_golestandt
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_golestandt
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: you know why nothing hurts gole outside her hollow? | ever hear why the stone dragon only bleeds in her lair
?B: no? | go on then
A: she and that hollow are one stone. the drovers call it the Bed. hit her anywhere else and the granite takes it
A: the giants out here are her kids. bits of the Bed that got up and walked
B: ...and we are sitting on dartmoor right now. great | so every giant we pulled today was family. nice
A: {name_b} tells it way better than me. ask in faction sometime

@topic fireside_apocalypse
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_apocalypse
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: know what the four riders up top have to do before they fight you? | fun fact about caer sidi while we sit here
?B: what | ask for a toll?
A: they have to ask. do you challenge fate. arawn's law. arthur said no and went home with six men
A: thats the bards' seven. the ones who walked out
B: and we said yes by walking in. cool. cool cool | so everyone in this group already answered
A: ask {name_b} for the full one sometime. the door shutting from the inside is the good part

@topic fireside_xanxicar
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_xanxicar
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: they used to sing the thing under here to sleep. every year | did you know a whole college sang over this cave once
?B: sing what to sleep | who did
A: the college of stars. three hundred years, longest night, a song called the Quieting. over xanxicar
A: morgana sang it as a student. then burned that college first
B: so nobody has sung it since. and here we are | that explains the mood down here
A: {name_b} has the whole story if you catch them in faction

@realm mid

@topic fireside_gjalpinulva
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_gjalpinulva
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: cold enough for you? thats her doing, you know | you feel that frost? it is not weather
?B: whose doing | then what is it
A: gjalpinulva wears the frost like a cloak. outside her court no blow lands on her. skalds say shes the wolf's daughter
A: the first svartalfar who met her eyes froze where they stood
B: so we dont look up. noted | and i thought it was just winter
A: get {name_b} to tell it properly some night. the werewolf king's answer is the best bit

@topic fireside_king-tuscar
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_king_tuscar
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the king up here made every weapon these giants carry. himself | you know tuscar is a smith, right? before anything else
?B: a giant blacksmith? | huh
A: apprentice to the giant who built asgard's wall. the one the gods never paid
A: best axe he ever made he gave to his queen. crossed the sea ice to hand it to her
B: romantic. for a thing trying to kill us | so the queen hits harder. good to know
A: {name_b} tells the whole saga. ask about the oath word on his hammer

@topic fireside_nosdoden
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_nosdoden
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: rule for down here. nobody stays dead on the floor. not for a minute | one thing while we rest. if i drop, rez me fast
?B: why the hurry | thats always the rule?
A: the worm at the bottom swallows the dead. they stand back up with their own faces and fight for it
A: but called back in time you keep your spirit. it only takes what is left lying
B: ok. rezzing fast. always | i am suddenly very fond of our healer
A: thats ketil grimsson's story. {name_b} tells all of it if you ask

@realm hib

@topic fireside_cuuldurach-the-glimmer-king
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_cuuldurach
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: see how the grass is grey up here? it was green once | these hills were just summer pasture, you know. before him
?B: before who | what happened to it
A: the glimmer king. one summer the sky tore and a pass opened that was not there the day before
A: the sage tyldifyl says sheeroe was always his. only the door is new
B: a door that opens can close. i hope | so we are trespassing. lovely
A: {name_b} tells it far better. ask for the King's Law

@topic fireside_olcasgean
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_olcasgean
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: dont drink the water in here, by the way | notice how every river on this isle bends toward this place
?B: why not | i did notice that
A: everything that drank it changed. the root at the bottom made this hollow. like a mouth
A: the forest pushed him here an age ago. but roots do not go away. they go down
B: so we are standing in his mouth. thank you for that | i was thirsty until now
A: {name_b} has the whole tale. the two trunks part is worth hearing

@topic fireside_black-lady
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_black_lady
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: you know the lady in here was only hired to sing at a funeral | she was a keener once. the one deeper in
?B: a singer? her? | and what went wrong
A: a keener never looks back at the grave. forty years she kept that. then they asked her to sing her own foster son
A: fourth night a voice from below asked why she should ever stop. and she looked back
B: ...ok that is sadder than i expected | and now she hates healers. i see it
A: ask {name_b} for it some evening. bring something to drink

@realm *

@topic fireside_legion
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_legion
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: you know why its called legion? | while we catch our breath. know where the name comes from?
?B: because theres a lot of demons? | no idea
A: two princes ran this place once. one ate the other and kept his voice. then ate everyone who challenged him
A: a hundred voices in one body now. and everyone who dies in his room heals him
B: so we do not die in his room. understood | i liked this place better before you told me
A: {name_b} tells the long version up top. worth asking

@topic fireside_grand-summoner-govannon
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_govannon
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the summoner at the bottom of this hall pays for everything he calls up | know what the sacrifice in the last room is for?
?B: pays who | i just kill it when told
A: its a bargain. sacrifice and demon walk to his feet. if both get there, his creditor comes up through the floor to collect
A: and hurt him enough and he drops the shape he wears. the demon steps out without a scratch
B: so kill the walkers. always | thats why everyone yells about the sacrifice
A: {name_b} tells where the shape came from. depends which realm you ask

# Ten more tales (2026-11-11, owner: "complete on all major bosses and encounters and lore"): the final bosses that had none.

@realm alb

@topic tale_aidon-the-archwizard
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_aidon-the-archwizard
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} who is the wizard on the stair in the hall of the corrupt | {name_b}, tell the aidon one
C: hush all, academy story | quiet in faction, this ones about the archwizard
D: go on {name_b}, my master wont say his name | please. the academy pretends he never existed
B: aidon was the first mage of the academy to master all four. fire ice earth, and the theurgists air
B: magus cerwyn tested him. a brazier, a basin, a stone, an open window. she wrote she would not see it done again
B: so the constable sent him to the pennine watch. to learn if the summoners wards on the road could be broken
?F: had nobody tried before | and he was the first to try?
B: magus idris tried before him. idris never came back
B: aidon worked above the watch. two apprentices carrying candles up in boxes of a hundred
B: and he learned what a ward is. a promise. every guardian stands there by a bargain. you pass a ward by answering it
~ 8
D: so what did he answer? | and what did they ask him for?
B: the summoners wanted a keeper against each of the four ways a road can be broken. he gave them four of himself
B: those are the reflections you fight. fire ice air earth. he can only pay again when all four are spent
?E: which is why you leave one walking. every raid leader screams it | leave one up. i have yelled that a hundred times
B: magus alun brought him down that way. two companies, keeping him one self short
B: the academy says he was deceived. the church says he sold the watch. the inconnu say they made an offer and waited
B: his letters still come up the stair. calm ones. promising the constable he will close the road for good
~ 25
F: one self short. thats horrible and i will remember it | so the fire around him is their seal. huh
C: he still writes letters. that part gets me | promising to close the road. every time

@topic tale_lord-gildas
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_lord-gildas
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} why does the lord at the bottom of the hall of the corrupt face us and not the summoners | {name_b}, the gildas one
C: quiet, this is the penhallow story | hush. hall of the corrupt tale
D: tell it {name_b}. my guild wiped to his poleaxe last week | please, i want to know who he was
B: gildas was second son of the house of penhallow. a squire at castle sauvage
B: he once held a breach in its wall for a night and a day. because nobody had told him he could leave
B: thats why the constable picked him for the pennine watch. he would hold the road and never act on his own judgment
B: the letter of appointment called that his great virtue
?F: sounds like a good soldier to me | whats wrong with that
B: twenty years nothing came up that road his watch could not turn back. the watch set its hours by his evening round
B: then the realm sent aidon. and gildas trusted him because the realm had sent him. he overruled his own captain
~ 8
D: and the order? theres always an order in these | so how did the watch end up dead at its posts
B: that last winter his men began wandering from their posts. so he gave the order. no man leaves his post for any reason
B: the summoners only had to keep his order for him. forever
B: thats why the dead watch cant be hurt a step past its posts. and why he is bound to the lowest point of the road
?E: pull them off their post and you hit air. ask me how i know | learned that one the expensive way
B: he died there the last night. shield up, facing the summoners hall. waiting for visitors who were already behind him
B: press him hard and he takes up the penhallow poleaxe. his family says you do that when only honour is left to guard
B: his grand niece dame morwen led the first company to bring him down. she goes back every spring until he knows her
~ 25
F: until he knows her. ok | nobody told him he could leave. twice
C: every spring. gods | i always go quiet at the grand niece

@topic tale_orylle
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_orylle
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} tell the one about the queen of krondon | {name_b} why does orylle throw people
C: shh, krondon story | quiet all, the ogre queen
D: yes please. i got thrown into a fire and nobody explained | go on {name_b}, the krondon one
B: orylle was born in the undercroft. the deepest seam of the ogres who dug under the isles before the hall folk built on them
B: she was the first of her people to climb up and look at what they had been digging under
B: she found krondon dying of age. its last elder counting empty chairs at the high table
B: she took the hall in one night without breaking a door. the elder died asking if she came as guest or enemy
?F: and which was it | did she answer him
B: then she walked every room. a ghost, the last teacher, translated the titles over the doors
B: and she gave every title to an ogre. the stores, the horn, the school, the road. thats why they all have work
~ 8
D: but the throwing? | and the fire?
B: hall folk guest law. a stranger who came in unannounced was set back on the guest stone to begin again properly
B: she hurls challengers down her hall onto that stone. into the fire burning on it. and fights only those who walk back
B: orshom brong drank the great hearth the night she took the hall. she made him champion and consort
?E: kill one and the other roars the name. loudest thing in albion | when one falls the other screams it. you dont forget
B: sir cador reached her first with twenty and was swept out. he came back with fifty chosen for stubbornness
B: and ice mages for the fire on the stone. they walked back every time. with the stone cold she throws no one
~ 25
F: chosen for stubbornness. my kind of raid | so you just walk back. every time
C: they say she wants neither to serve nor to rule. only to keep | guest or enemy. she never did answer

@topic tale_duraek-the-empowered
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_duraek-the-empowered
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} whats wrong with the drakoran lord in avalon city. fire heals him?? | {name_b}, tell the one about dura'ek
C: quiet please, avalon city story | hush, {name_b} is telling the empowered
D: please. our wizard nuked him back to full last night | go on, i need to know what we did wrong
B: dura'ek was one war lord among five when avalon burned. lord of the dry'ak, the clan that holds doors
B: one thing set him apart. he kept more sworn protectors than any other lord. every one bound to die before he does
B: morgana gave his clan the doors. he took the chancellors court at the heart of the city
B: a woman saw him standing on the steps there. listening to the paving
?F: listening to what | whats under the paving
B: under it lay the stair down to the crystal cave. and what sleeps there
B: on the third night the readers saw a cold light rise from the city. and he went down alone
~ 8
D: and came back how? | what did the dragon do to him?
B: nobody agrees. the clans say xanxicar gave him a gift. his own captured men say he stole from a sleeper
B: the readers say he only touched something the dragon lay on. he came up at dawn burning
B: xanxicar has two heads and no breath. dura'ek has two breaths now. fire and frost feed him
?E: no fire no frost. say it with me | NO FIRE NO FROST. every pull
B: thats the cry sir kenrick brought him down to. and his six protectors died before him. as they had sworn
B: he forbids the dragons name in his court. he wants to be a lord in his own right
B: and every sentry on the stair below says it anyway
~ 25
F: so our wizard healed him. great | no fire no frost. writing it on my hand
C: he forbids the name and they all say it. i like that bit | listening to the paving. brr

@realm mid

@topic tale_aros-the-spiritmaster
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_aros-the-spiritmaster
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} why does the spiritmaster in dodens gruva shout his own name | {name_b} tell the aros one
C: hush, mine story | quiet all. dodens gruva
D: tell it. i heard him yelling through two walls | {name_b} please, the mine one
B: aros was jarl ormarrs spiritmaster. trained in the craft of hels servants. binding spirits to serve
B: he believed one thing above all. a good name never dies. and a name said aloud is a rope that holds a soul to the world
B: every morning at the shaft he read the names of the shift. and promised none would be forgotten
?F: thats kind of nice actually | sounds like a good man to work for
B: then a warning was ignored. the picks broke into the cold seam
B: the miners heard voices in three tongues calling from the hall below. and died
B: and their dead began to walk down toward the call. so aros bound them. to keep them
~ 8
D: bound how? | and the name?
B: he made each of them say HIS name. so they would hear his voice louder than the calling. thats why he still cries it at you
B: he raised bjorn the younger, the strongest of the shift, as his champion
B: and he holds the bound souls in himself. when he spends them they burst out in a storm that empties the room
?E: the storm. yes. back off when it comes | emptied my whole group once
B: the jarl went down after the dead with forty huscarls. aros followed him down the stair shouting names
B: and turned him back. dead
B: he still reads the names every morning. when the calling below stops the miners may go. he says he has forgotten how
~ 25
F: so die in there and he learns your name | he keeps them. i dont love that
C: none would be forgotten. he kept the promise. thats the awful part | every morning. still

@topic tale_iarnvidiur
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_iarnvidiur
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} who is the old woman in the iron wood really | {name_b}, the iarnvidiur one tonight?
C: quiet, aegir story | hush all. the iron wood
D: please. the dwarves spit when i ask | go on {name_b}, nobody on aegir will tell me
B: depends who tells it. jordheims skalds say she is the giantess of the old songs. east in the iron wood, breeding fenrirs kin
B: the iarn dwarves only say she was on aegir before their first clan
B: and the narfi of her lair say she was young when the iron trees were silver and sang. before a rot they will not name
?F: so which came first, her or the rot | did she make the rot?
B: the dwarves say her plague made the rot. the narfi say the rot made her
B: her first litter guards the lair. hati and skoll lie at her door. named for the moon chaser and the sun chaser
B: above ground her servants walk the wood looking like anyone. and the dwarf clans lose children to them
~ 8
D: has anyone killed her? | can she even be hurt?
B: her plague is her blood. it eats everything near her and it closes her own wounds
B: vemunds thirty were the first company in her lair. they could never wound her deeply enough to trouble her
B: ragnheid grimsdottirs warband did it. with dwarf guides. they went down carrying more cures than weapons
?E: brewed from the bark of the iron trees. tastes like a forge | more cures than weapons. still true
B: and she has a habit. anything that hurts her enough to be a nuisance she sets in the black water under the bridge
B: the way a woman sets a pup back in its basket
B: she comes back. the iron wood has always had an old one. she is waiting for the wolves to run at the end of the world
~ 25
F: a pup back in its basket. thats what we are to her | more cures than weapons. ok
C: some grandmothers say gjalpinulva is her daughter. just saying | waiting for the wolves. i hate that she is patient

@topic tale_queen-kula
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_queen-kula
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} tell the one about the queen in the glacier | {name_b}, kula tonight?
C: hush, tuscaran story | quiet all, the ice queen
D: yes. i only know to kill her and the king together | please {name_b}, the long one
B: kula is the youngest and coldest of bergelmirs line, the skalds say. the rime giant who stayed north when her brothers went south
B: why she stayed depends who you ask. jordheim says she wanted endless winter. her cast out sculptors say she was left behind
B: the dwarves say she was sent
?F: sent by who | thats the worst of the three
B: she found a dragon dead in the ice of delling crater. so vast nothing could thaw it
B: and raised tuscarans citadel on its bones. cutting around a sleeper in the north wall
B: a dead kings army came up from the south to take the bones. she stilled it with a touch and a breath of sleep. and gave it orders
~ 8
D: and tuscar? | where does the king come in
B: tuscar was a smith. he came courting with an axe and she married him
B: for a time the two were bound so closely that a wound to one closed the others
B: she ruled by one law. only the merciless live through a winter
?E: which is why you burn them down together. ask any raid leader | together or not at all. yes
B: and she keeps a cold older than the gods in reserve. the giants named it thors might. as a joke
B: the first warband to reach the thrones was told to its face that her guardians were useless. and lost
B: a hundred under bergljot steinsdottir won. the queens crown of ice hangs at bjarken. unmelted
~ 25
F: a wound to one closed the others. thats almost sweet | came courting with an axe. midgard
C: when she dies the throne room cracks. the skalds say the ice remembers her name | unmelted. still

@realm hib

@topic tale_avartack-the-champion
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_avartack-the-champion
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} who is the champion before the hall in marfach | {name_b} tell avartack tonight
C: hush, breifine story | quiet in faction, the ferrymans son
D: please. he would not die and i want to know why | tell it {name_b}, the ford and all
B: avartack was the son of aed dub. the ferryman who kept the ford of the erne
B: he grew up fighting in the water. where a man cannot step back or aside. only reach
B: he was fostered beside the boy who became caimheul. the day caimheul was made chieftain he named his foster brother champion
?F: so they grew up together? | brothers then, near enough?
B: twenty years he held the fords of breifine in single combat. never lost in the water
B: he kept the law of the water. the ford belongs to whoever faces it. and a turned back may be struck down without shame
B: his oath was this. i will stand before you until you have no need of me
~ 8
D: thats a fine oath. isnt it? | whats wrong with the oath?
B: it has no word in it to end the watch
B: the day caimheul died on the reed flats, avartack was away. holding the ford of the erne
B: he came home to the bier. went under the hill first. and stood at his lords feet in the grave chamber, facing the door
B: he died on his feet in the third night. so on the fourth, when it happened, he did not need to stand up
?E: and he is whole again the moment nobody stands against him | someone always faces him. always
B: he takes the floor before the hall for the ford. the first company came at him in a ring and broke at the back
B: echna of ardee, a ferrymans daughter, faced him and never turned. her sister on her bank, her company at his sides
B: when he fell she said the old word that ends a watch. it did not hold. but the ferrymen call it over the water at night
~ 25
F: no word to end the watch. oof | so you face him and you do not turn. ok
C: he did not need to stand up. every time | they call it over the water. i like that they still try

@topic tale_chieftain-caimheul
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_chieftain-caimheul
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} tell the one about the chieftain in marfach | {name_b}, caimheul?
C: quiet, this ones ours | hush. the crooked mouth
D: go on. my grandfather called him ours and wouldnt say more | the chieftain, {name_b}. please
B: caimheul ruled the breifine hills before there were keeps on them
B: thats not the name his mother gave him. a lake mans knife left his mouth crooked and the hills forgot the other
B: he was a hard lord. burned booleys, kept hostages. his people loved him anyway
B: because no reaver took a cow from his valleys that he did not take back twice over
?F: so a cattle lord? | hard how?
B: he taught his sons to fight with a stick in the dust of the yard
B: the man in front meets the shield and reels. the man who wont reel he mocks until he comes on careless
B: and the man at his side, where he cannot see. that one he kills first. with the long spear
~ 8
D: and the hostages? | what happened on the reed flats?
B: he took nine hostage children of the lakes. when the peace broke they died of a coughing sickness in his hostage house
B: only a keener in red sang for them
B: years on, on the reed flats, a herd boy named mochta threw a spear into his side. his sister had been one of the nine
B: his champion was away that day. holding a ford
?E: stand at his flank and you die first. the verse says so | never at his side. front or nowhere
B: he was sung back up and does not hear the voice below at all. he takes every stranger for the lake men
B: crochnat of howth heard the old yard verse at the muster. drew something in the dust. and brought him down the next night
B: when he casts the shield aside he is hurt deep and thinks you are about to break. be ready then
~ 25
F: he holds their road because he thinks its his country | so he doesnt even know. hm
C: the keeners added a verse. asking him to find mochta and the nine and say he is sorry | he was ours. thats the hard part

