B: you know the first verse. king of the fomorians. an eye poisoned by his fathers druids cauldron that destroyed whatever it saw
B: he shut his daughter away on tory against a prophecy. her son lugh drove the eye out through his skull at mag tuired
B: it fell facing his own host. and destroyed it
?F: everyone knows that part | and thats the end?
B: the sylvan know a second verse. the eyes bearers wrapped it in seven hides and carried it west. walking backwards
B: the fomorians say it followed its people of its own will
B: on the shore of hy brasil the hides slipped. it looked on a valley for one breath
~ 8
D: gleann glas? | what was in the valley?
B: a sylvan village. gleann glas. it burned, and everything else in the valley. thats the vale of balor
B: on the crag above they built tur suil around it. one window
B: and grew a king around the eye again. with a household
?E: his hide turns everything and he wont bleed outside his chamber | and then the roof opens. you will see
B: as he weakens an eye opens in the roof, beyond any weapon. it chooses one of those below and burns them until it shuts
B: eochaidh of ardee was chosen at the last. fiachna of howth brought the king down the next spring
B: carrying a smooth stone for lughs sake. every company that climbs tur suil carries one since
~ 25
F: i am finding a smooth stone tomorrow | it chooses one. great
C: walls do not hold everything. thats how the book ends | and the vale glows red more often. they say

